bin/
.venv/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.exe

# Cross-compiled control-plane binaries. They are build products (GOOS=linux
# go build, see deploy/kubernetes/tai-talea-control-plane.yaml) that get
# pushed as an image, roughly 19 MB each. Anchored to the repository root so a
# future script that merely starts with the same prefix is not swallowed.
/tai-talea-linux
/tai-talea-linux-*

# The assembled offline runtime bundle is a build product, several gigabytes
# each, and several of its members are past the per-file limit a git host
# allows. The recipe that produces and verifies it lives in
# provision/wheelhouse, and the bundle itself belongs in an artifact store.
provision/wheelhouse/out/
provision/wheelhouse/dist/

# The local wheel slot holds artifacts that no public index can serve -- the
# internal sglang fork, wheels built from a source-only pin. They stay out of
# the repository on purpose: tai-talea is public and that fork is not, so
# committing them would publish internal patches. Point local_wheels.paths at
# an artifact store instead; the reasoning is in provision/wheelhouse/README.md.
provision/wheelhouse/wheels/*.whl
provision/wheelhouse/wheels/*.tar.gz
provision/wheelhouse/wheels/*.zip
